# Custom core overlay - ESP32-CAM_MJPEG2SD (XIAO ESP32S3 Sense + OV5640)
#
# Raises the lwip TCP send buffer above the IDF default of 5760 bytes.
#
# Why: MJPEG streaming throughput is send_buffer / RTT. At 5760 bytes over a
# 7ms link that is ~820 KB/s theoretical and ~600 KB/s measured, which caps the
# stream at 8.4 fps with 69KB frames while the sensor is supplying 30. Measured
# cost model (COM4, two frame sizes): time/frame = 17ms fixed + bytes / 720KB/s.
# Confirmed by the streamSkipped counter: sent + skipped = 598 offered per 20s,
# exactly the 30fps capture rate, with the sender dropping the difference.
#
# The value: 45952 = 32 x CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_MSS (1436). Holds 2.3 MB/s even at a
# degraded 20ms RTT, and stays well under the 65535 hard cap that applies
# because CONFIG_LWIP_WND_SCALE is off. lwip pbufs prefer PSRAM on this core
# (mem_clib_malloc is heap_caps_malloc_prefer, SPIRAM first), so the memory cost
# lands in PSRAM - where it competes with camera frame buffers - not internal heap.
#
# NOT changed here: CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_WND_DEFAULT is the RECEIVE window and does
# nothing for outbound streaming. Raising it only speeds inbound transfers (the
# OTA .bin POST) and would have to be paired with CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_RECVMBOX_SIZE
# >= 32. Separate experiment, separate justification.
#
# How to apply: append to configs/defconfig.esp32s3 in esp32-arduino-lib-builder
# at commit 2f061cb, built against esp-idf release/v5.3 @ cfea4f7c98 and
# arduino-esp32 @ 9eb7dc6f. That is the exact combination recorded in
# versions.txt of the stock esp32-arduino-libs for arduino-esp32 3.1.1, so a
# build with only this line added should differ from stock in only this value.
CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_SND_BUF_DEFAULT=45952

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REPRODUCTION RECIPE (validated 1 Sep 2026, five failed attempts to get here)
#
# lib-builder pinned to 2f061cb, and these three MUST be pinned by hand because
# lib-builder resolves them forward and they had drifted ~21 months:
#   components/arduino               -> 9eb7dc6f   (git checkout)
#   components/arduino_tinyusb/tinyusb -> 249556360 (git checkout)
#   main/idf_component.yml esp_matter -> "==1.3.0"  (was "^1.3.0", caret resolves
#                                        forward to a breaking API)
#   main/idf_component.yml esp32-camera -> 4335c93e (was git "master"; forward
#                                        drift silently switched the SCCB I2C
#                                        driver and the camera task stack size)
# Then: source esp-idf/export.sh && ./build.sh -s -t esp32s3
# ESP-IDF is pinned by build.sh itself with -i cfea4f7c98 on the first run.
#
# Verify with check-sdkconfig-drift.sh before flashing anything. A correct build
# differs from stock ONLY in CONFIG_LWIP_TCP_SND_BUF_DEFAULT plus build-metadata
# strings (ARDUINO_IDF_BRANCH/COMMIT) and unrelated mdns/libsodium options.
